@startuml
title Rios Vivos — proposed self-hosted RAG architecture
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor "Authorized internal\nuser" as user
rectangle "Rios Vivos application boundary" {
  [Web / Admin client] as client
  [system-api\nAuth, ACL, jobs, audit] as api
  database "PostgreSQL\nmetadata, ACL, document versions,\njob state, audit" as pg
  queue "Redis / durable queue\ningestion + query jobs" as queue
  [Authenticated\nWebSocket gateway] as ws
}

cloud "Private source storage\nS3 OR encrypted AI-host disk\noriginal files + versions" as objectstore

node "Private AI host\n4th-gen Intel Core i7\nGTX 680 optional; CPU-first baseline" {
  [Worker] as worker
  [Text extraction / OCR] as extract
  [Local multilingual\nembedding service] as embed
  database "Self-hosted vector index\nchunk vectors + document/version IDs" as vector
  [Local quantized\nanswer model] as llm
}

user --> client : upload / question
client --> api : HTTPS + authenticated session
api --> pg : authorize; create/read job
api --> queue : enqueue only after authorization
api --> ws : publish persisted job state
ws --> client : authorized progress/result event
client --> api : poll fallback; download citation

worker --> queue : reserve idempotent job
worker --> pg : read ACL scope, metadata; write status/audit
worker --> objectstore : read authorized source version
worker --> extract : extract + normalize
extract --> embed : chunks
embed --> vector : vectors + provenance metadata

worker --> vector : retrieve using API ACL allow-list
worker --> llm : question + authorized passages only
llm --> worker : grounded answer + cited chunk IDs
worker --> pg : store result/citations/status

note bottom of api
The vector index is not an authorization boundary.
API-derived document/version filters are mandatory.
end note

note bottom of vector
Derived, rebuildable data. Originals and ACLs
do not live only in the vector index.
end note
@enduml
